Knowledge Level: Level 2 (PR)
Document source: [PR 016_2023 - Aktivitas Pengadaan Barang dan-atau jasa (inbound logistics) - OCR.pdf](https://365tsel.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/ProcurementAssuranceandComplianceDepartment/IQDRr3nccyn0T5XdV-MKPhUxAbUagWQ7_T7vquP3TY5TKaM?e=EhzbN1)

Based on the documents **Procurement Hub Agent** can access, the preparation of *Demand Planning* is carried out by the *User* Function in coordination with other relevant corporate functions, such as the *Finance Business Partner* and Procurement Functions, in accordance with Article 4 of Director's Regulation No. 016/LO.01/FN-00/VIII/2023 (*Peraturan Direktur Keuangan dan Manajemen Risiko Perseroan*) concerning *Aktivitas Pengadaan Barang Dan/Atau Jasa (Inbound Logistics)*.

In general, the stages of *Demand Planning* activities consist of the following:
- Ensuring information regarding program approval for the Goods and/or Services to be listed in the initiative list within the RKAP (*Rencana Kerja Anggaran Perseroan*) or other required documents;
- Detailing the requirements for Goods and/or Services down to the *Bill of Quantity* (BoQ) level, *Item* level, or functionality level;
- Checking the availability of existing Agreements (*Perikatan*) for the required Goods and/or Services;
- Approving the list of initiatives in the *Demand Planning*;
- Verifying the details of the Goods and/or Services required and stated in the initiative list to determine whether to proceed via a *Sourcing* process or Purchase Requisition–Purchase Order (PR-PO).

Furthermore, Article 4 Paragraph 2 outlines the relationship and linkage of *Demand Planning* with other procurement activities as follows:
- *Demand Planning* can serve as the foundational information for executing *Category Management* activities;
- *Demand Planning* is used as the foundational information for carrying out *Sourcing* activities or amendments to Agreements (*Perikatan*);
- *Demand Planning* can serve as the foundational information for conducting *Joint Procurement* activities.

